\section{Day states}{

Every day has exactly one of three states (DECISIONS.md, D-015):
\itemize{
\item \strong{training}: the load of the day is greater than 0;
\item \strong{rest}: the load of the day is 0;
\item \strong{missing}: the load of the day is not available (\code{NA}).
}

Sessions on the same day are summed. If any session of a day has an \code{NA}
load, the whole day is \code{NA} and its state is "missing": a missing load is
never silently replaced (D-016).
}

\section{Gap rule}{

Each athlete's calendar runs from their own first to their own last date.
Days in between that have no row are added and marked \code{filled = TRUE}.
By default (\code{gaps = "rest"}) they are treated as rest days with load 0;
with \code{gaps = "missing"} they get load \code{NA} and state "missing" (D-015).
The calendar ends at the athlete's last row: rest days after the last
session are not added, so trailing rest days must be given as rows with
load 0 to be included.
A message reports how many days were filled. Whatever \code{gaps} is, a warning
is given for every run of more than \code{max_gap} consecutive filled days,
because a long run without data is as likely to be missing data as rest.
}

